		<div class="flex py-16 flex-col md:flex-row">
			<div class="grow">
				<div class="md:sticky md:top-[var(--header-height)]">
					<a href="/changelog/2026-10-01-desktop-v1.14.4/" class="font-semibold text-3xl sm:text-xl">
						October 1, 2026
					</a>
					<div class="font-mono mt-2 text-muted">
						<a href="/changelog/2026-10-01-desktop-v1.14.4/" class="flex items-center gap-4">
							<span class="text-sm">1.14.4
								
									<span span class=""> Desktop</span>
								
							</span>
						</a>
					</div>
					<div class="mb-8 mt-3 text-xs text-muted font-mono">
						
							<a href="/pricing#catalyst"><span class="bg-accent-900 text-accent-300 py-0.5 px-2 rounded-xl">catalyst</span></a>
						
					</div>
				</div>
			</div>
			<div class="md:basis-3/4">
				
				<div class="typeset break-words" dir="ltr">
					<h2>Improvements</h2>
<ul>
<li>Bases: Added “Hide column” to the right-click menu of a kanban column.</li>
<li>Bases: A base made with “Create new base” now names its first view “View” instead of “Table”.</li>
<li>Search in the File Explorer, Bookmarks, Outline, and Sync views now matches the full path of each item. Excluding a term (e.g. <code>-Archive</code>) now hides a matching folder and everything inside it.</li>
<li>The <strong>Outline</strong> and <strong>Outgoing links</strong> views now work for files opened from outside the vault.</li>
</ul>
<h2>No longer broken</h2>
<ul>
<li>Bases: Fixed “Copy path” showing up below “Delete” when you right-click a file in a table, cards, or kanban view.</li>
<li>Bases: Fixed a base failing to load when a view’s <code>groupOrder</code> is not a list.</li>
<li>Bases: Fixed “Add group” in the <strong>Group</strong> menu not adding a group when selecting a link suggestion.</li>
<li>Fixed property suggestions sometimes showing results for an earlier query, which made <code>Enter</code> pick an old link instead of what you typed.</li>
<li>Fixed a memory leak in the metadata cache after opening and editing external files.</li>
</ul>

				</div>
			</div>
		</div>
		
